@overheard dinner
// Writer 4, batch 8. The mess at dinner (and some breakfasts), where you spend the most time. Every department,
// mixed tables. The food, the days off, the weekend, home, tonight's tradition, the season, kind gossip. At most
// one in five about work.

== overheard
// ---- the food ----
? place:mess act:dinner pair:works+galley
A: What is it tonight?
B: {dish}.
A: Is there more?
B: There's always more. Take a plate.   #warm

? place:mess act:dinner pair:any+any
A: Is that {dish}?
B: It is.
A: Then it's a good day after all.   #warm

? place:mess act:dinner pair:survey+watch
A: Have you tried the pudding?
B: Twice.
A: You're only allowed once.
B: I was very polite the second time.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner pair:friend
A: Swap you my roll for your pudding.
B: No.
A: Two rolls.
B: ...Still no. Nice try.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner pair:any+any
A: Pass the salt?
B: Brennan says it doesn't need salt.
A: Brennan's not looking.
B: She's always looking.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner pair:comms+helm
A: Is this the same soup as Tuesday?
B: Better. It's had two days to think.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner pair:infirmary+works
A: Eat your greens.
B: Is that doctor's orders?
A: It's aide's orders. They're stricter.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner pair:any+any
A: Who makes the gravy like this?
B: Brennan. Her mum's way, I heard.
A: Tell her mum thank you.   #warm

? place:mess act:breakfast pair:any+any
A: Toast or porridge?
B: Yes.
A: That's not an answer.
B: It's the right answer.   #funny

? place:mess act:breakfast pair:bunk
A: You're up early.
B: I smelt the bacon from Deck 4.
A: There isn't any bacon.
B: Then I dreamt it. Still worth getting up.   #funny

// ---- days off and the weekend ----
? place:mess act:dinner weekday:fri pair:works+any
A: Weekend tomorrow?
B: Two whole days. I've got nothing planned.
A: Lovely.
B: I'm going to do it very well.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner weekday:fri pair:friend
A: Lie-in tomorrow?
B: Till nine. Maybe ten.
A: I'll save you a breakfast.
B: You're a real friend.   #warm

? place:mess act:dinner weekday:sun pair:any+any
A: Back to it tomorrow.
B: Don't.
A: Sorry. Nice weekend, though?
B: Lovely. Too short. Always too short.

? place:mess act:dinner pair:bunk
A: What are you doing on your day off?
B: Garden. Book. Nap.
A: In that order?
B: In any order. That's the point.   #funny

? place:mess act:breakfast weekday:sat|sun pair:any+any
A: Nobody's rushing today.
B: Weekend breakfast. Best breakfast.
A: Another tea?
B: Go on, then.   #warm

// ---- home ----
? place:mess act:dinner pair:friend
A: Did you get through to home?
B: Second try. Everyone's well.
A: Good. That's good.
B: My sister's got a new job. I'm proud.   #warm

? place:mess act:dinner pair:any+any
A: This tastes like my gran's cooking.
B: Is that good?
A: It's the best thing anyone could say.   #warm

? place:mess act:dinner pair:survey+any
A: What's it like at home this time of year?
B: Cold. Windy. Lovely.
A: You miss it.
B: I miss the soup.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner who:silva-bea|soto-marta|jovanovic-petra with:silva-bea|soto-marta|jovanovic-petra
A: What's your number tonight?
B: Higher than yesterday. Yours?
A: Same. Higher. Pass the bread.

? place:mess act:dinner who:ueda-vera with:varga-tariq
A: Did the post bag come?
B: Next week, they say.
A: Six weeks, every time.
B: Makes the letters taste better.   #warm

// ---- tonight's tradition ----
? place:mess act:dinner trad:quiz pair:any+any
A: Quiz after this. Are you on our team?
B: Only if I'm not on the song round.
A: You're on the song round.
B: Then no.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner trad:jam pair:any+any
A: Music night later.
B: Are you singing?
A: Everyone's singing. Nobody agrees on the words.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner trad:observatory-night pair:any+any
A: Observatory after dinner?
B: Bring a flask.
A: And biscuits.
B: Obviously biscuits.   #warm

? place:mess act:dinner trad:film pair:friend
A: Film night. Is it the long one?
B: It's always the long one.
A: I'll bring the big cushion.
B: I'll bring the other big cushion.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner trad:running pair:any+any
A: Running club after this.
B: After all this pudding?
A: Especially after.
B: Then I'll walk. Briskly.   #funny

// ---- the seasons ----
? place:mess act:dinner season:sowing pair:any+any
A: Have you planted yours?
B: Yesterday. In a pot on the windowsill.
A: Mine's up already.
B: Show-off.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner season:greening pair:garden+any
A: Greens from the garden tonight.
B: You can tell. It tastes greener.
A: That's not a taste.
B: It is now.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner season:harvest pair:any+any
A: Is this the garden's squash?
B: Grown upstairs. Well, downstairs. Deck 3.
A: Tastes like it knows us.   #warm

? place:mess act:dinner season:lanterns pair:friend
A: Have you made your lantern yet?
B: It's lopsided.
A: They're meant to be.
B: Then mine's perfect.   #funny

// ---- kind gossip ----
? place:mess act:dinner pair:comms+any
A: Did you hear? Someone's got a birthday tomorrow.
B: Who?
A: I can't say. But there's a cake in the cold store.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner pair:friend
A: Have you seen the new comic on the wall?
B: The one with the coffee machine?
A: It's got a face. A grumpy face.
B: It's very accurate.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner who:santos-zofia with:tran-chloe
A: Guess who beat the rowing board today.
B: I don't gossip.
A: ...
B: Fine. Who?   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner pair:any+any
A: Someone left a thank-you cake for the galley.
B: Who?
A: Nobody knows. Brennan nearly smiled.   #warm

? place:mess act:dinner who:dlamini-lukas with:esposito-yara|madsen-ivo|walsh-esme
A: Two hundred and something.
B: Days?
A: Days.
B: We'll miss you when it's zero. Pass the jug.   #warm

// ---- named tables ----
? place:mess act:dinner who:halloran-emeka with:yoon-elif|lemaire-nils|yilmaz-karin
A: Why was the soup so cheerful?
B: Go on.
A: It was in high spirits.
B: That's terrible. Save it for breakfast.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner who:mensah with:holt
A: Good dinner, Chief.
B: Hm. Adequate.
A: You had seconds.
B: Adequate seconds.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner who:kim-yusuf with:garcia-greta
A: Your headphones working?
B: You fixed them last week.
A: Just checking. Mine aren't.
B: Give them here. Eat your dinner.   #warm

? place:mess act:dinner who:alvarez-luca with:mbeki-bo
A: My sister sent a recipe.
B: So did mine.
A: Shall we ask Brennan?
B: One at a time. She's got a face for two.   #funny

// ---- work, once or twice ----
? place:mess act:dinner pair:works+works
A: Board was heavy today.
B: Then it'll be light tomorrow.
A: You always say that.
B: And I'm always half right.   #funny

? place:mess act:dinner pair:watch+survey
A: Long shift?
B: Long enough. Are those potatoes?
A: Roast. Sit down. We'll talk after.   #warm
